{"type":"standard","title":"Ty Masterson","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ty Masterson</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q7859620","titles":{"canonical":"Ty_Masterson","normalized":"Ty Masterson","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ty Masterson</span></span>"},"pageid":23490861,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/TY_mASTERSON_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-TY_mASTERSON_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":464},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/TY_mASTERSON_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":614,"height":864},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1380105798","tid":"ed1d7f45-c745-11f1-bff3-10b35248fe0c","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:37:37Z","description":"American politician (born 1969)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Masterson","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Masterson?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Masterson?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ty_Masterson"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Masterson","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ty_Masterson","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ty_Masterson?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ty_Masterson"}},"extract":"Ty Masterson is an American politician who is the president of the Kansas Senate. A member of the Republican Party, he has represented the 16th district since 2009. From 2005 to 2008, he was a representative in the Kansas House of Representatives. He lives in Andover and served on the Andover City Council.","extract_html":"<p><b>Ty Masterson</b> is an American politician who is the president of the Kansas Senate. A member of the Republican Party, he has represented the 16th district since 2009. From 2005 to 2008, he was a representative in the Kansas House of Representatives. He lives in Andover and served on the Andover City Council.</p>"}